Functions that fall off the end without returning a value. Many are
UNUSED stubs; others call a function whose result MWCC leaves in r3, so
the original code "returns" it by accident. clang treats flowing off the
end as undefined behaviour and may trap or drop code (wasm), so the host
build returns the intended value (or a zero value for unused stubs).
This also fixes declarations whose return type disagrees with the
definition or caller (ObjUtility::getPtrMainLocaleArc, the driver.cpp
CheckAndLoadAnimSoundAvailable redeclaration, main returning int) and
include paths whose letter case only works on case-insensitive disks.

